description:
FILED s531c (Opus agent, 2026-11-01), from #4020's probes.  PRE-EXISTING (base ade297e7 identical).  SILENT WRONG (rare spellings; no board row known).

    package Foo; sub bar {} package main;
    my $g = *Foo::; print "1 $g\n";
    print "2 ", (\%Foo:: == \%Foo:: ? "same" : "diff"), "\n";
    print "3 ", ref(*Foo::{SCALAR}), "\n";
    print "4 ", "" . *main::, "\n";
  perl 5.40.3: 1 *main::Foo:: / 2 same / 3 SCALAR / 4 *main::main::
  PCL:         1 1            / 2 diff / 3        / 4 HASH(0x3)
Probe: scratch/s531c/p/stash4.pl in the s531c worktree.

Mechanism: the spelling `*Pkg::` (and `%Pkg::`) compiles to `(p-stash "Pkg")`, a FRESH snapshot hash per evaluation (ir-spec "The stash as a hash"), so a stash glob VALUE is a hash table: in scalar context it is its count (`my $g = *Foo::` -> 1), stringified it is `HASH(...)`, two `\%Foo::` are two tables.  s531c (#4020) taught p-glob-slot that such a value IS a stash glob (`%p-stash-glob-pkg`: a hash in *p-stash-pkg-table*, or an empty-named typeglob from `*{"Pkg::"}`) for the HASH / NAME / PACKAGE / GLOB slots; the glob VALUE itself (its string, its scalar-context value, its identity) and the SCALAR slot are this task.  Fix shape to measure: the scalar-context / stringify readers of a p-stash view answer the glob name `*main::Pkg::` (one predicate, %p-stash-glob-pkg), and `\%Pkg::` returns one cached view per package (identity) -- inside the s522 deferral (a live stash object stays deferred).
